cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use SimplAr in your work, please cite it as below.
type: software
title: "SimplAr: desktop tools for 40Ar/39Ar geochronology"
abstract: >-
  Desktop tools for 40Ar/39Ar geochronology, from the laboratory's data export
  to plateau, isochron and combined ages: data conversion, flux-monitor
  reduction, J regression across the irradiation disk, step-heating plateau and
  isochron ages, age distributions with mixture and minimum-age models, and
  recalculation of published ages between calibrations.
  Every age carries analytical, internal and external uncertainties.
authors:
  - given-names: Joakim Gyrup
    family-names: Hansen
    affiliation: Natural History Museum of Denmark, University of Copenhagen
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-7604-7202"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Joakim-SNM/SimplAr"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
  - geochronology
  - 40Ar/39Ar
  - step heating
  - isochron
  - flux monitor
